1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,921
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:43,961
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,880
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,679
[♪ upbeat music playing]

7
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,234
EPISODE 5

8
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:12,447
[cell phone vibrating]

9
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,449
Hmm?

10
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:18,245
Good morning, Mr. Choi.

11
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:20,205
Good morning.

12
00:01:20,289 --> 00:01:21,582
[Isoo] What made you call so early?

13
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,875
I booked a consultation for you.

14
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:27,671
[sighs] I told you I don't like shrinks.

15
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:30,591
What if I get hypnotized again
and do something? I'm not going.

16
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:32,759
I'm worried about you.

17
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:35,053
Why do you worry so much? Huh?

18
00:01:35,137 --> 00:01:36,930
Didn't you see me catch those hitmen?

19
00:01:37,014 --> 00:01:38,432
Nothing bad happened.

20
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:40,475
Just listen to me.

21
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:42,311
Ignoring it won't make it go away.

22
00:01:42,394 --> 00:01:44,146
You get yourself checked out first.

23
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,690
Ignoring indigestion won't make it better.

24
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:47,941
[sighs in exasperation]

25
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:50,736
Will you go if I go?

26
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,405
Of course. You go first, then I'll go.

27
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,324
I have to go to work now. Bye.

28
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:56,908
[line disconnects]

29
00:01:58,577 --> 00:01:59,786
[sighs in exasperation]

30
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:00,996
[sets down phone]

31
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:02,622
[inhales]

32
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:04,666
[exhales deeply]

33
00:02:15,302 --> 00:02:16,386
[elevator dings]

34
00:02:21,183 --> 00:02:22,184
[digital beep]

35
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:29,149
[exhales softly]

36
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:31,151
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

37
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:32,319
[audio distorts]

38
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:33,654
[muffled metallic clinking]

39
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:35,530
[high-pitched tone droning]

40
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,201
[groans]

41
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:40,744
[thud]

42
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,206
[slow heartbeats]

43
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:47,918
[groans]

44
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:52,255
-[elevator clunks]
-[grunts]

45
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:54,800
[breathing heavily]

46
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:57,803
[metallic clinking intensifies]

47
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:01,139
[high-pitched ringing intensifies]

48
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:05,143
[panting]

49
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:06,311
[audio normalizes]

50
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:10,565
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

51
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:19,908
[inhales]

52
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:21,660
[elevator dings]

53
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,120
[continues panting]

54
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:32,838
[♪ music fades]

55
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,716
ROSEBUD HOTEL

56
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,844
-[woman] I'm so excited!
-[chuckles]

57
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,262
[♪ quirky music playing]

58
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,806
-Welcome.
-Hello.

59
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,724
-We made a reservation.
-Yes, we did.

60
00:03:44,808 --> 00:03:46,184
May I have your name?

61
00:03:46,268 --> 00:03:47,519
Lee Gwanghui.

62
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,479
-Lee Gwanghui?
-[keyboard clacking]

63
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:52,232
-Why are you so cute today?
-Because today's a special day.

64
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:53,984
Really? Oh...

65
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,611
I'm sorry, but I can't seem
to find your reservation.

66
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,697
What? Uh...

67
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,615
Then please try "Oh Gyeonghwa."

68
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:02,284
-Please.
-Oh Gyeonghwa.

69
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:03,535
Even her name's pretty.

70
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,078
[Gyeonghwa giggles]

71
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:07,164
-[keyboard clacking]
-[couple chattering indistinctly]

72
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,958
I'm sorry,
but I can't find your reservation.

73
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:12,794
-What?
-What's going on, babe?

74
00:04:13,712 --> 00:04:16,381
That can't be right.
I'm sure I made a reservation. I...

75
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:20,594
I think I canceled to get
a lower rate and never rebooked.

76
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:24,222
Ah. Forget it. I'm leaving.

77
00:04:25,015 --> 00:04:26,224
Wait, hold on.

78
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:27,809
So...

79
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:30,854
Could you perhaps save me?

80
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,022
I mean,

81
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,065
do you have any rooms left?

82
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:35,692
On White Day? As if.

83
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:37,486
One moment, please.

84
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:39,780
Everyone's walking around with candy.

85
00:04:39,863 --> 00:04:41,281
I assumed mine was in the room.

86
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,658
-I really hope you have a room.
-Yes, we have one.

87
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:45,994
You do? We'll take it.

88
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:47,496
The last room on the seventh floor.

89
00:04:47,579 --> 00:04:49,873
-Thank you. They had a room.
-Thank you.

90
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:52,167
-You're so annoying!
-Come on.

91
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,378
At least make an effort.

92
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,381
[clicks tongue]

93
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:01,510
I wish you'd forget what happened earlier.

94
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:04,012
-I can't forget it.
-Babe.

95
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,889
It's our one-year anniversary.

96
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:07,557
I wish you would.

97
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,310
I'll let it slide.

98
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,229
[groans affectionately] You're so cute.

99
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:16,650
[sighs] What am I supposed to do
if you're this cute even when you're mad?

100
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,777
I can't help it. I was born this way.

101
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,779
-I think I'm trapped.
-Me too.

102
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:23,281
-Please save us!
-Save us!

103
00:05:23,365 --> 00:05:24,407
[elevator dings]

104
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:26,117
[Gwanghui] We're saved. [chuckles]

105
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,412
Wait, stop.

106
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:31,248
We can't just go like this.

107
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,124
-Here, hold this.
-Hmm?

108
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:34,876
[clears throat, spits]

109
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:36,962
[squeals]

110
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:38,922
[grunts]

111
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:41,675
-What are you doing?
-[panting]

112
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:42,884
My knees...

113
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:45,428
It's our anniversary today.

114
00:05:45,512 --> 00:05:47,931
So your feet won't be touching
the ground all day.

115
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,015
Okay!

116
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:50,851
[♪ quirky music playing]

117
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:55,814
Now, where are we?

118
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:59,985
-Am I heavy?
-[continues panting] No.

119
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:02,904
You're light as a feather.

120
00:06:02,988 --> 00:06:05,282
You should stop losing weight.

121
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,492
-You're lighter than a strand of hair.
-Okay.

122
00:06:07,576 --> 00:06:09,619
-Now, where is our room?
-Over there.

123
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:11,204
Here we are!

124
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:12,873
-Okay!
-Here?

125
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:14,332
Yes, go on.

126
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,543
-Go on.
-Wait.

127
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,253
Hold it properly for it to...

128
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:20,088
-Try placing it carefully.
-Okay.

129
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:21,256
-[card reader beeps]
-It worked!

130
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:22,424
It worked!

131
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:23,884
-It worked!
-It worked.

132
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:24,968
Here we go!

133
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:26,386
-[exclaims excitedly]
-[panting]

134
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:27,679
-It's gorgeous.
-This room is amazing.

135
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:29,764
[shrieks] It's so beautiful!

136
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:31,683
-It's beautiful.
-Yes, it's so beautiful.

137
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,936
-[grunting]
-Isn't it great?

138
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,229
[♪ ominous sting]

139
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,481
-[exclaims]
-[squeals]

140
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:41,484
Babe, you're so manly!

141
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:43,445
Babe! Are you leaving?

142
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:48,325
[♪ ominous sting]

143
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:49,951
[screaming]

144
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,959
[sighs] They really shouldn't have
sent me all these.

145
00:06:58,043 --> 00:06:59,085
Honestly.

146
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:01,087
Kyungjin.

147
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:02,589
Ooh, what's that?

148
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,132
It's for White Day.

149
00:07:04,758 --> 00:07:06,468
-Thank you.
-Detective Park...

150
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:07,636
PARK JUNYOUNG

151
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:12,557
He took a day off on White Day?

152
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,267
That's very fishy.

153
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:15,602
What is?

154
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:18,647
My exceptional detective instincts
are kicking in.

155
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:23,485
That clueless Detective Park who only
listens to trot music is dating someone?

156
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:26,029
-He said he's meeting his mom.
-Right?

157
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,865
Who would date someone like him?

158
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,408
I'm sure he went to see his mom.

159
00:07:30,492 --> 00:07:31,951
[♪ quirky music playing]

160
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:33,203
Is it White Day today?

161
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:34,996
-[Kim Suwon] Yes.
-[Byungsik exclaims]

162
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,706
I forgot last year, too.

163
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:37,791
Hey.

164
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:41,169
-Got any cash?
-Just pay by card.

165
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,462
I use my wife's card.

166
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,255
[Kim Suwon] Do I look like I have money?

167
00:07:44,339 --> 00:07:45,548
Lend me 20,000 won.

168
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,176
Come on, just 20,000 won.

169
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:49,386
Just 20,000 won.

170
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,180
[whispers] He's surprisingly devoted.

171
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:54,307
[whispers] I heard
his wife is really scary.

172
00:07:54,391 --> 00:07:55,517
[gasps]

173
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:57,769
What about you?

174
00:07:57,852 --> 00:08:00,522
[sighs] I've already got my surprise
all planned out.

175
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,565
You're so diligent. A true romantic.

176
00:08:02,649 --> 00:08:04,776
-Aren't you going to date, bro?
-Hey.

177
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,404
I prefer to meet people naturally.

178
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,155
Look at these. That's...

179
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:12,951
It's a new case.

180
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:16,788
We got a report of a body. Rosebud Hotel.

181
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:20,583
-Yes! You what?
-Today, I--

182
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,585
What about White Day?
The case comes first.

183
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:23,712
Okay, let's go.

184
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,506
-[Kyungjin] Come on.
-The case should come first.

185
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,508
[Kyungjin] But, bro, seriously...

186
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,180
We're with Gangha Police.

187
00:08:34,264 --> 00:08:36,891
ROSEBUD HOTEL CONCIERGE
JEON YUJIN

188
00:08:36,975 --> 00:08:37,976
Right.

189
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,686
I'm the general manager.

190
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,104
ROSEBUD HOTEL GENERAL MANAGER
YU JONGYEOL

191
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,188
Hello.

192
00:08:42,272 --> 00:08:43,857
[♪ enthralling music playing]

193
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:47,902
Where's the scene?

194
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,029
In Room 709.

195
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:51,823
[chuckles]

196
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:52,907
[gasps]

197
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:56,202
[♪ quirky music playing]

198
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,704
Detective Park.

199
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,290
What are you doing here?

200
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:01,875
I called him.

201
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:03,835
Why? It's his day off.

202
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,503
The case comes first.

203
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:07,964
Dr. Yoon?

204
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:09,549
Dr. Yoon from Forensic Pathology? Oh!

205
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:13,178
Gosh, Detective Jin.
Fancy meeting you here.

206
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:14,429
[Isoo] What are you doing here?

207
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:17,182
I have plans, obviously. [chuckles]

208
00:09:17,766 --> 00:09:19,100
I was actually on my way out.

209
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:20,560
This is perfect timing.

210
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:22,187
-A body was found here.
-What?

211
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,772
-Come with us.
-But I...

212
00:09:23,855 --> 00:09:25,023
You're here.

213
00:09:26,066 --> 00:09:27,400
-[Dr. Yoon] Oh.
-Yeah.

214
00:09:27,484 --> 00:09:29,277
You were here, too. [chuckles softly]

215
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,528
Hello, Dr. Yoon.

216
00:09:30,612 --> 00:09:31,613
Dr. Yoon.

217
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,531
We've met before.

218
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:35,408
Oh, yes, Detective Joo.

219
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,618
[chuckles]

220
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,369
I look forward to working with you.

221
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:39,579
Likewise.

222
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:41,498
Please follow me.

223
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:43,458
Come on, let's go.

224
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,794
-Let's go.
-[clears throat] Yes, let's go.

225
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:49,881
So Dr. Yoon is his mom?

226
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:51,716
Did you see that? They were linking arms.

227
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,635
-They jumped apart in surprise.
-[giggles]

228
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:56,262
-What plans did they have at a hotel?
-[Kyungjin] Drumroll.

229
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:02,811
This is the place.

230
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:04,354
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

231
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,700
It looks like she's been dead for a while.

232
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:20,495
It's been at least 12 hours.

233
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,456
It looks like she was stabbed.

234
00:10:26,918 --> 00:10:29,337
-In three places.
-Right.

235
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:34,634
She was stabbed in three places,
but there's not much bleeding.

236
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:36,761
[sighs]

237
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:39,514
Bleeding can be minimal.
It depends where you were stabbed.

238
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:42,600
-I'll check during the autopsy.
-Okay.

239
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:47,730
Her phone.

240
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:57,782
[Kyungjin] I don't see the murder weapon.

241
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:01,828
-Get this to forensics.
-Yes, ma'am.

242
00:11:04,873 --> 00:11:06,749
-Hello, sir.
-Detective Joo.

243
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:11,504
We can't find the murder weapon,
and there's little blood.

244
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:13,339
-I'll take a look.
-Okay.

245
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:16,593
-You stay here, Detective Park.
-Got it.

246
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:23,308
Do you know the victim?

247
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,894
Her name's Oh Minyeong. She a concierge.

248
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,813
Where is the person who found the body?

249
00:11:28,897 --> 00:11:30,106
They're at the bar.

250
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,691
This way, please.

251
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:37,697
-What?
-Are you even human?

252
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,616
I am. I'm human.

253
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,451
I'm drinking because I'm human.

254
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:42,952
You're worse than an animal.

255
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:45,788
Don't talk that way.
Have some manners in a place like this.

256
00:11:45,872 --> 00:11:48,499
-You're seriously saying that right now?
-Babe.

257
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:50,418
-Hello.
-Gosh, you startled me.

258
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,008
Aren't you Jin Isoo?

259
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,635
Yes, I am.

260
00:11:58,718 --> 00:11:59,719
[shrieks excitedly]

261
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:02,347
Oh my god. You're so good-looking.

262
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,098
He's not that good-looking.

263
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,308
No one asked you, ugly.

264
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,060
[Gwanghui] Ugly?
You've got to be kidding me.

265
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,686
Can I get a photo with you?

266
00:12:08,770 --> 00:12:10,104
-Why not?
-[Gyeonghwa] Thank you.

267
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:11,439
-Ugly, huh?
-I'll take it.

268
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:12,523
Thanks.

269
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:14,525
One, two, three.

270
00:12:14,609 --> 00:12:15,944
[Gwanghui] Don't stand too close.

271
00:12:16,027 --> 00:12:17,237
-[camera shutter clicks]
-[squeals]

272
00:12:18,488 --> 00:12:20,156
Oh, uh, is she your girlfriend?

273
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,075
Gosh, of course not.

274
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:23,284
We're police.

275
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:24,786
[Isoo] I'm here to work.

276
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:26,955
You found the body, didn't you?

277
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:28,790
Can you explain what happened?

278
00:12:30,625 --> 00:12:34,879
We started dating on White Day last year.

279
00:12:34,963 --> 00:12:37,382
So I made a reservation
for our one-year anniversary,

280
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:39,759
but there was a bit of a problem.

281
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,469
You were too cheap to book it.

282
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:44,305
You're really going to humiliate me
in front of other people?

283
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:45,515
I said it was a mistake.

284
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:46,683
And?

285
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:50,270
Ah, so our reservation was canceled,

286
00:12:50,353 --> 00:12:53,189
but it turns out they had one room left.

287
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:56,109
They had a room left on White Day?

288
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:57,568
They would've been overbooked.

289
00:12:57,652 --> 00:12:58,861
No, they had a room left.

290
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:03,032
So I carried my adorable baby

291
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:04,575
and walked down the hallway.

292
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:07,412
Yes, exactly.
It was straight out of a movie. [chuckles]

293
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:09,038
Since we're on the subject,

294
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:11,249
you were a little heavier
than you used to be.

295
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:14,335
-I almost threw my back out.
-You said I was as light as a feather.

296
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:15,712
Don't be ridiculous.

297
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:17,297
Hey, Mr. Ugly.

298
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:19,132
Let's focus here.

299
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:21,467
-Yes, Mr. Ugly.
-Right.

300
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:24,304
So we opened the door like this,

301
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:26,681
but then, some woman

302
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,058
was right there behind the bed,
like a ghost.

303
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:30,810
With her eyes wide open.

304
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:33,646
So we just ran out of there.

305
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:38,568
Why leave out the part where
you threw me onto the bed? Embarrassed?

306
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:41,195
[scoffs] You're bent on making me
look like a coward, aren't you?

307
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:42,780
I told you, I was just startled.

308
00:13:42,864 --> 00:13:45,742
Exactly. You ditch your girlfriend
when you're startled.

309
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:47,160
I just panicked for a second.

310
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,037
-Enough. I'm upset.
-And I'm humiliated!

311
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,246
Okay, focus.

312
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:54,000
Did you touch anything inside the room?

313
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,209
Or see anything strange?

314
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,712
No.

315
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:58,921
Nothing like that.

316
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,257
Thank you for your cooperation.

317
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:02,550
We may contact you again.

318
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,634
Okay.

319
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,178
[Isoo inhales sharply]

320
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,388
-He looks familiar.
-[Gyeonghwa] Bye.

321
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,475
You and I are over!

322
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:12,268
How many times must I apologize?

323
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,395
-Fine, blame me for being a coward.
-[Isoo sighs]

324
00:14:14,479 --> 00:14:16,272
It's like watching a soap opera.

325
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:17,482
That's why I don't date.

326
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:19,734
Isn't it that you can't?

327
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:22,820
With this face?

328
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:25,406
[scoffs]

329
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:27,617
She's the narcissistic one.

330
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:30,036
[whispers] She's unbelievable.

331
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,663
Just go. Don't let my screaming stop you.

332
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:39,295
We've prepared a suite for you.

333
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:40,880
Please stay as long as you like.

334
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:42,340
[♪ dramatic music playing]

335
00:14:44,342 --> 00:14:45,343
During your stay,

336
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:48,805
all hotel services, including
food and beverages, are complimentary.

337
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,350
-Including alcohol?
-Of course.

338
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,643
[gasps]

339
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:54,727
Get up.

340
00:14:54,811 --> 00:14:56,562
You love free stuff, babe.

341
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,564
-[Gwanghui] Let's go.
-[Gyeonghwa giggles]

342
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:02,610
[sighs]

343
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:03,694
Jeez.

344
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,446
[scoffs]

345
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:07,115
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

346
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,451
I don't think I saw her
after 7:00 p.m. last night.

347
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:11,536
Right?

348
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:13,246
Yes, that's right.

349
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:19,961
Do you know anyone who might've had
a grudge against Ms. Oh Minyeong?

350
00:15:23,214 --> 00:15:25,007
I'm not sure.

351
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:29,262
Did she have any trouble
with any guests at all?

352
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:32,849
[chuckles nervously]

353
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,309
[clears throat]

354
00:15:37,562 --> 00:15:41,149
The hotel was all red and glossy,
but why is the back of house like this?

355
00:15:41,732 --> 00:15:44,861
What about the staff?
They have rights too, don't they?

356
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:45,945
Wait.

357
00:15:47,238 --> 00:15:49,323
-I'll be right back.
-Where are you going?

358
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,033
To canvass the area.

359
00:15:54,162 --> 00:15:56,956
HOUSEKEEPING

360
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,124
[knocking]

361
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,209
-[housekeeper 1] Yes?
-Excuse me.

362
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:01,335
[♪ quirky music playing]

363
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:02,587
-Goodness.
-He's handsome.

364
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:05,298
-Aren't you the heir of Hansu Group?
-You're right.

365
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:06,632
Oh...

366
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:08,634
You ladies have a sharp eye.

367
00:16:08,718 --> 00:16:10,469
Hear that? He called me a lady.

368
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:12,471
-It was me.
-No, it was me, silly.

369
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:16,309
What's a chaebol heir doing
all the way down here?

370
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:19,812
I'm in charge of Ms. Oh Minyeong's case.

371
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:22,356
-Ah...
-"In charge of"?

372
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,691
He's a detective.

373
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,776
He rammed a helicopter
into a car last year.

374
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,778
Yes, that was me.

375
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:30,364
-[chuckles] I think I saw that, too.
-[housekeeper 1] Right?

376
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:31,616
Excuse me.

377
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:34,035
Did Minyeong really die?

378
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:38,915
Yes, so I was wondering if I could get
some help from you lovely ladies.

379
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:42,543
Gosh, you keep calling us ladies
and flattering us like that.

380
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:45,087
Ow! You're pretty strong.

381
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:47,882
Try working here for three months,
you'll bulk right up.

382
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:49,800
We're all wearing matching outfits.

383
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:51,510
-You're right.
-Me too.

384
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:53,971
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

385
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:07,068
Detective Joo.

386
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:09,111
This is Ms. Oh Minyeong's shift log.

387
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,821
You should take a look at this.

388
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:11,906
[housekeeper 1] Minyeong?

389
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:14,325
Men just wouldn't leave her alone.

390
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:16,244
She's gorgeous.

391
00:17:16,327 --> 00:17:19,413
Being pretty isn't easy. I would know.

392
00:17:19,497 --> 00:17:21,374
I was quite the catch back in the day.

393
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:23,542
-You're still beautiful.
-[scoffs playfully]

394
00:17:23,626 --> 00:17:27,213
Honestly, you have good taste.
[chuckles]

395
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,675
I think some of the staff
asked her out as well.

396
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:31,759
-[housekeeper 1] Really?
-Yeah.

397
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,095
Have you seen anyone suspicious lately?

398
00:17:34,804 --> 00:17:36,514
-Anyone suspicious?
-Were there any?

399
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:38,474
[murmuring quietly]

400
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,184
Ah!

401
00:17:40,268 --> 00:17:41,602
-Room 701.
-The ugly guy?

402
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:42,979
-Yes.
-Room 701?

403
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:46,482
I heard he's a chaebol heir.
He's been in the suite for three weeks.

404
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:47,733
And?

405
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:50,528
He kept calling for Minyeong,

406
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,071
saying he had requests to make.

407
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,155
[housekeeper 2] That's right.

408
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:56,701
He stared at her in this creepy way
and followed her around.

409
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:57,785
Right.

410
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:58,953
That funny-looking man.

411
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,663
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

412
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:02,164
Funny-looking?

413
00:18:03,749 --> 00:18:05,543
He called for her multiple times a day.

414
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:07,086
REMARKS
ATTENDED TO ROOM 701

415
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:09,338
Who is the guest in Room 701?

416
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:12,883
That guest is confidential,
so I can't say.

417
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,803
Do you have cameras on the seventh floor?

418
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,016
The camera on the seventh floor

419
00:18:20,850 --> 00:18:22,852
-is off.
-Why?

420
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:26,772
It broke down two months ago,
but it hasn't been repaired yet.

421
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:31,152
A five-star hotel just left
a broken security camera?

422
00:18:31,694 --> 00:18:33,446
That doesn't make sense to me.

423
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:36,782
[Jongyeol] Uh...

424
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:39,744
A maintenance report wasn't filed.
It was a mistake.

425
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,373
[♪ music fades]

426
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:47,710
You two meet with Ms. Oh's family
and break the news.

427
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:49,670
See what they have to say.

428
00:18:49,754 --> 00:18:51,172
-Got it. Let's go.
-Got it.

429
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:57,428
[line connects, ringing]

430
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:01,140
[cell phone vibrating]

431
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:03,809
[♪ gritty blues-rock music playing]

432
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:05,519
SHADOW WITHOUT A TRACE
TRACK TO THE END

433
00:19:05,603 --> 00:19:06,937
JEONG MINJAE DETECTIVE AGENCY

434
00:19:07,021 --> 00:19:08,648
HYERA

435
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:10,358
[cell phone continues vibrating]

436
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,195
Hey, it's been a while.

437
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,614
Yeah. How's the business going?

438
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:19,450
It looks like word got around.
I've been swamped.

439
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:21,702
[chuckles] I have a favor to ask.

440
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:22,870
What is it?

441
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:24,372
Rosebud Hotel.

442
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:28,042
It's a murder case, but the security
camera on the seventh floor is down.

443
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:31,545
I need you to use the backdoor
to find out when and how it went offline.

444
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:33,464
I told you I'm busy.

445
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:35,383
It'll take you 10 minutes.

446
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:36,884
Five minutes.

447
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:38,803
-Gopchang?
-Deal.

448
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,513
-I'll call you later.
-Okay.

449
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,556
-[line disconnects]
-[hurried footsteps approaching]

450
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,266
-[Isoo] Detective Joo!
-Yeah.

451
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,351
[in English] Big news!

452
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,062
-[in Korean] Did you learn something?
-Of course.

453
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,147
There's a suspect
in the seventh-floor suite.

454
00:19:50,231 --> 00:19:52,650
Yeah, he kept calling for Ms. Oh.
Let's go meet him.

455
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:53,943
Let's go.

456
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:07,373
Chunsik?

457
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:08,499
Oh.

458
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:10,626
Isoo!

459
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:13,045
KANG CHUNSIK
SOLE HEIR OF CHUNSIK FOOD

460
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,715
-"Isoo"?
-[Isoo] Yeah.

461
00:20:16,257 --> 00:20:18,592
This is Kang Chunsik,
the sole heir of Chunsik Food.

462
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:20,177
[softly] Oh.

463
00:20:20,261 --> 00:20:22,012
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

464
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:24,515
He looks old,
but he's two years younger than us.

465
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:25,933
He was born in 1994.

466
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:28,519
What a nice thing to say
first thing in the morning.

467
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:29,979
Morning, huh?

468
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,480
It's 5:00 p.m. Anyway, go inside.

469
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:32,898
-Why?
-Come inside.

470
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:33,983
What's going on?

471
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:39,280
[Isoo] Whoa...

472
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,615
Look at the state of this room.

473
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,202
THE PERSON I FELL FOR
AT FIRST SIGHT IS...

474
00:20:45,286 --> 00:20:46,829
[Chunsik] Something sad
happened yesterday.

475
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:48,873
[Isoo] Something sad?

476
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:50,416
What was it? Tell me.

477
00:20:54,128 --> 00:20:55,421
What do you know about love?

478
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,381
Forget it.

479
00:20:57,465 --> 00:20:58,466
[scoffs]

480
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:01,635
You've been here three weeks.
Did you run away from home?

481
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:02,845
No, I just...

482
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:04,555
I just came.

483
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,932
Is it because of Ms. Oh Minyeong?

484
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:11,979
Why are you asking about Ms. Oh Minyeong?

485
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:14,273
Her shift log says
you kept calling for her.

486
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:17,568
Oh...

487
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:21,238
I had requests to make, but why...

488
00:21:23,574 --> 00:21:24,742
Wait, who are you?

489
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:28,496
She's a detective.
Be straight with us. I'm a detective, too.

490
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:31,207
I didn't do anything wrong.

491
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:34,418
Then why did you keep calling for her?

492
00:21:34,502 --> 00:21:35,961
Were you stalking her?

493
00:21:36,045 --> 00:21:38,339
Stalking? What are you talking about?

494
00:21:38,422 --> 00:21:39,757
[angrily] I wasn't!

495
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:45,262
[sighs softly]

496
00:21:45,846 --> 00:21:47,223
I fell for her at first sight.

497
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,771
[♪ gentle jazz music playing]

498
00:21:56,607 --> 00:21:59,026
Here is the vase you requested.

499
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:11,121
Do you need anything else?

500
00:22:21,465 --> 00:22:22,466
[♪ music fades]

501
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:25,886
That's what people call stalking.

502
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:28,097
And your face already screams "suspect."

503
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,849
I'm not bad-looking.

504
00:22:30,683 --> 00:22:32,101
Right?

505
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:33,644
Uh...

506
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:34,937
No comment.

507
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,897
[Isoo] Don't you look in the mirror?

508
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:40,484
I told you to work on your looks
if you want to date. Just look at you.

509
00:22:40,568 --> 00:22:43,946
I am working on my looks.
Do you know how expensive my clinic is?

510
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:47,116
Excuse me, please tell us
what happened yesterday.

511
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:50,536
Yesterday...

512
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:55,833
I asked her out.

513
00:22:56,792 --> 00:23:00,880
I couldn't hide my feelings anymore.

514
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:03,716
If she said yes,

515
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:05,259
today would be our anniversary.

516
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:08,929
We'd be a White Day couple.

517
00:23:10,556 --> 00:23:11,849
[mumbles]

518
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:13,309
With that?

519
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:16,562
Hey, that's from that movie.
It was a whole thing 20 years ago.

520
00:23:17,271 --> 00:23:18,439
[Chunsik] Come on.

521
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:20,733
I had the perfect plan.

522
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:24,862
I want to confess my feelings
to the person I love.

523
00:23:25,446 --> 00:23:27,907
[chuckles] How can I help with that?

524
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:29,783
Uh...

525
00:23:29,867 --> 00:23:31,827
I need flowers, balloons, and a cake.

526
00:23:31,911 --> 00:23:34,413
What kind of cake would you like?

527
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:35,497
I'm not sure.

528
00:23:35,873 --> 00:23:37,416
Um...

529
00:23:37,499 --> 00:23:40,336
What flavor do you like, Ms. Oh?

530
00:23:41,921 --> 00:23:45,341
I'm clueless about what women like.
[chuckles]

531
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:48,385
Our hotel is famous
for our chocolate cake.

532
00:23:49,303 --> 00:23:50,846
Then please prepare that.

533
00:23:50,930 --> 00:23:51,931
Of course.

534
00:23:52,014 --> 00:23:53,766
[♪ gentle, pleasant music playing]

535
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,787
[inaudible conversation]

536
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:33,347
Then I'll take my leave now.

537
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:34,473
Hold on.

538
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:37,977
I need to rehearse.

539
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:40,854
Could you sit here for a moment?

540
00:24:41,522 --> 00:24:42,731
Just for one minute.

541
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:44,483
[♪ music fades]

542
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:45,609
[chuckles softly]

543
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:47,069
Please, this way.

544
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,242
Please sit here.

545
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:54,326
Okay.

546
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:08,132
[♪ dreamy retro music playing]

547
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:12,678
[sharp exhale]

548
00:25:14,763 --> 00:25:16,140
I HAVE FALLEN IN LOVE

549
00:25:16,223 --> 00:25:17,975
I have fallen in love.

550
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:22,312
I've never felt this way before.

551
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:24,815
I'm feeling a little shy.

552
00:25:33,323 --> 00:25:35,325
She came to me with the scent of flowers.

553
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:38,954
You must be wondering who she is.
[chuckles]

554
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,878
The person I fell for at first sight is...

555
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:51,842
It's you, Minyeong.

556
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:55,971
Minyeong.

557
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:57,681
I'm sorry. I have a boyfriend.

558
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:02,144
Minyeong...

559
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:03,520
-[♪ music fades]
-[door opens]

560
00:26:03,604 --> 00:26:05,314
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

561
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:07,649
Another one, please.

562
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,200
[sobbing]

563
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,536
One more.

564
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:20,621
[♪ music fades]

565
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:24,541
Just like that,

566
00:26:25,876 --> 00:26:28,003
the love of my life left me.

567
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:31,799
What time did you call
Ms. Oh Minyeong here?

568
00:26:31,882 --> 00:26:32,883
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

569
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:33,967
Around

570
00:26:34,885 --> 00:26:36,053
seven o'clock?

571
00:26:37,137 --> 00:26:38,388
What time did she leave?

572
00:26:38,472 --> 00:26:39,473
About

573
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:41,975
Forty minutes later.

574
00:26:43,519 --> 00:26:45,687
Did she report me?

575
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:49,983
I really didn't stalk her.
My feelings are sincere.

576
00:26:51,944 --> 00:26:53,153
[sighs deeply]

577
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:56,532
Ms. Oh Minyeong has died.

578
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:57,866
What?

579
00:26:57,950 --> 00:27:00,702
She was murdered last night.

580
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:06,166
Chunsik.

581
00:27:06,917 --> 00:27:07,918
Mr. Kang.

582
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:10,003
-[Isoo] Chunsik.
-Wake up, Mr. Kang.

583
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:12,422
Mr. Kang, wake up.

584
00:27:12,506 --> 00:27:13,632
[Isoo] Hey, hey...

585
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,384
[Hyera sighs]

586
00:27:16,844 --> 00:27:17,845
[sniffs]

587
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:19,429
This is alcohol.

588
00:27:20,264 --> 00:27:21,557
-So it is.
-Isoo.

589
00:27:22,182 --> 00:27:25,185
[coughs] You're lying, right?

590
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:26,854
Please tell me it's a lie.

591
00:27:27,688 --> 00:27:28,689
It's a lie, right?

592
00:27:29,815 --> 00:27:31,775
Come on, Detective.

593
00:27:32,401 --> 00:27:34,403
What in the world is going on?

594
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,363
You're a detective, Isoo!

595
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:38,448
[sobbing]

596
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,535
Minyeong!

597
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:53,714
[sighs softly]

598
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,382
[Chunsik continues sobbing]

599
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:57,217
Stop crying!

600
00:28:00,888 --> 00:28:03,515
Did Ms. Oh Minyeong have a boyfriend?

601
00:28:03,599 --> 00:28:04,725
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

602
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:05,976
Uh...

603
00:28:06,059 --> 00:28:07,561
I'm not sure.

604
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:12,065
I don't know either.

605
00:28:14,234 --> 00:28:17,237
Did anyone stay in Room 709 last night?

606
00:28:17,321 --> 00:28:20,324
No, Room 709 was unoccupied.

607
00:28:20,991 --> 00:28:22,117
It was unoccupied?

608
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:25,078
Why did she go
to an unoccupied room alone?

609
00:28:25,162 --> 00:28:26,705
[♪ music swells, fades]

610
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:32,002
[sobbing, ragged breathing]
Why did our daughter...

611
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:34,379
Why did she die?

612
00:28:34,463 --> 00:28:36,214
[♪ melancholy music playing]

613
00:28:38,884 --> 00:28:40,093
[Minyeong's dad] Who did this?

614
00:28:41,637 --> 00:28:43,347
We're still investigating the matter.

615
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:45,265
[continues sobbing, breathing raggedly]

616
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:50,312
Did your daughter

617
00:28:50,896 --> 00:28:52,773
have a boyfriend?

618
00:28:55,484 --> 00:28:57,653
It did seem like
she was seeing someone lately.

619
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:59,529
She even received an expensive handbag.

620
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:02,199
I think it was one of the hotel staff.

621
00:29:02,282 --> 00:29:04,868
Did her boyfriend kill her?

622
00:29:04,952 --> 00:29:06,119
We don't know yet.

623
00:29:07,788 --> 00:29:08,789
By any chance,

624
00:29:09,498 --> 00:29:11,041
was there anyone

625
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:13,126
who might've had a grudge against her?

626
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:14,920
Our daughter was the sweetest girl!

627
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:16,672
There isn't anyone like that!

628
00:29:20,968 --> 00:29:24,721
Can we take a look around her room?

629
00:29:24,805 --> 00:29:26,515
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

630
00:29:42,030 --> 00:29:43,740
[♪ music increases in tempo]

631
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:55,002
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

632
00:29:56,086 --> 00:29:57,713
This has to be worth a fortune.

633
00:30:04,845 --> 00:30:06,221
Oh.

634
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:07,514
This is a limited edition.

635
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:17,566
You can't buy this with money.

636
00:30:21,570 --> 00:30:22,946
[♪ music swells, fades]

637
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:26,533
SEWON HOSPITAL

638
00:30:34,541 --> 00:30:36,460
The name is Choi Jeonghun.

639
00:30:36,543 --> 00:30:38,295
[receptionist] Please wait just a moment.

640
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:52,476
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

641
00:30:58,315 --> 00:31:00,108
[monitor beeping steadily]

642
00:31:11,078 --> 00:31:12,329
[♪ music fades]

643
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:17,209
[clears throat softly]

644
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:20,670
-Mr. Choi Jeonghun?
-Yes.

645
00:31:20,754 --> 00:31:22,714
-You're all done with your tests.
-Okay.

646
00:31:22,798 --> 00:31:26,009
We sent your biopsy for analysis,
so the results will take a few days.

647
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:28,261
Let's get you booked in.

648
00:31:28,345 --> 00:31:29,387
All right.

649
00:31:29,471 --> 00:31:31,431
These two dates are available.

650
00:31:33,767 --> 00:31:35,644
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

651
00:31:43,777 --> 00:31:44,861
ROOM 709

652
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:47,572
[Hyera] She went into
an unoccupied room and died.

653
00:31:49,241 --> 00:31:50,242
Why?

654
00:31:54,121 --> 00:31:55,622
[cell phone vibrating]

655
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:00,460
Hey.

656
00:32:00,544 --> 00:32:02,337
That camera on the seventh floor

657
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:04,172
isn't broken. It was turned off.

658
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:06,299
It was blocked by the central server.

659
00:32:06,967 --> 00:32:08,593
January 14, at 8:00 p.m.

660
00:32:08,677 --> 00:32:09,761
MANUAL RECORDING STOP

661
00:32:09,845 --> 00:32:11,596
Okay, thank you.

662
00:32:15,100 --> 00:32:19,437
Someone manipulated the camera
and planned this murder?

663
00:32:20,981 --> 00:32:22,315
REPORTING PARTY

664
00:32:22,399 --> 00:32:23,733
LEE GWANGHUI
OH GYEONGHWA

665
00:32:25,402 --> 00:32:26,403
VICTIM, ROOM 701 GUEST

666
00:32:26,486 --> 00:32:28,697
OH MINYEONG, AGE 31
KANG CHUNSIK, AGE 30

667
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,448
It had to be someone on the inside.

668
00:32:33,368 --> 00:32:35,912
Detective Joo.
Here's the crime scene report.

669
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:39,166
This is just the fingerprints
and trace evidence.

670
00:32:39,249 --> 00:32:42,335
-We'll go over the bloodstains tomorrow.
-Okay. Thank you.

671
00:32:42,961 --> 00:32:43,962
Aren't you going home?

672
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:45,922
I will in a bit. You go on home.

673
00:32:46,006 --> 00:32:47,465
-Okay, bye.
-Bye.

674
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:57,392
[♪ music fades]

675
00:32:57,475 --> 00:33:01,104
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

676
00:33:07,569 --> 00:33:10,322
Someone's a real workaholic, aren't they?

677
00:33:10,405 --> 00:33:11,781
[yawning]

678
00:33:12,699 --> 00:33:14,576
-What time is it?
-It's 9:00 a.m.

679
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:17,621
-At least sleep at home.
-[sighs]

680
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:21,208
-The report came out?
-Yeah.

681
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:28,673
No trace of Chunsik's fingerprints.

682
00:33:29,299 --> 00:33:30,592
Chunsik's out.

683
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:34,471
We don't know that. They wiped the handle.

684
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:36,556
Go wash up before you come closer.

685
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:41,269
Hydrogen peroxide was on her clothes.

686
00:33:41,353 --> 00:33:43,146
VICTIM'S CLOTHING
HYDROGEN PEROXIDE DETECTED

687
00:33:43,230 --> 00:33:44,689
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

688
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:48,735
They also found reddish-brown fibers.

689
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:58,078
[♪ music increases in tempo]

690
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:05,377
[♪ music fades]

691
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:12,050
[Dr. Yoon] Light over here, please.

692
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:16,680
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

693
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:21,559
[cell phone vibrating]

694
00:34:21,643 --> 00:34:22,644
Who is it?

695
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,898
It's Detective Joo Hyera.

696
00:34:26,982 --> 00:34:28,400
[Dr. Yoon] Put her on.

697
00:34:29,526 --> 00:34:30,527
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

698
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:31,695
[on speakerphone] Hello? Dr. Yoon?

699
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:33,196
Have you started the autopsy?

700
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:34,948
Yes, just now.

701
00:34:35,031 --> 00:34:37,033
Do we have an estimated time of death yet?

702
00:34:37,117 --> 00:34:39,619
Between 8:00 and 9:00 p.m.

703
00:34:39,703 --> 00:34:40,704
And the murder weapon?

704
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:41,788
Uh...

705
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:43,748
It's a knife,

706
00:34:44,708 --> 00:34:46,710
but not a kitchen knife.
The blade's thinner.

707
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:53,758
The blade is about 16 mm wide.

708
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:58,054
It has a serrated edge.

709
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:10,900
[sobbing]

710
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:21,620
He's still going around like that?
What's with his clothes?

711
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:25,248
Is it true love?

712
00:35:26,541 --> 00:35:28,627
Or the crocodile tears of a killer?

713
00:35:33,381 --> 00:35:35,216
Hey, why are you buying so much bread?

714
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:36,760
It's a tasty bribe.

715
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:38,720
I've got my informants everywhere.

716
00:35:38,803 --> 00:35:39,804
Informants?

717
00:35:40,430 --> 00:35:41,806
Can you go pick up the coffee?

718
00:35:41,890 --> 00:35:43,266
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

719
00:35:54,903 --> 00:35:55,904
We'll take this, too.

720
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:58,031
[bakery clerk] Yes,
I'll get it ready for you.

721
00:35:58,114 --> 00:36:00,241
Their chocolate cake is famous, remember?

722
00:36:01,117 --> 00:36:02,118
Really?

723
00:36:04,996 --> 00:36:06,122
[♪ music fades]

724
00:36:06,206 --> 00:36:07,332
Who are your informants?

725
00:36:08,208 --> 00:36:10,210
The people who are
invisible to the guests,

726
00:36:10,293 --> 00:36:13,588
but know everything that happens here.

727
00:36:13,672 --> 00:36:16,883
You know you can't pay people
for information, right?

728
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:19,386
You think I'm an idiot?

729
00:36:19,469 --> 00:36:20,720
Just follow me. [clicks tongue]

730
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:23,973
-[housekeeper 1 sighs]
-[knock at door]

731
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:25,058
Yes.

732
00:36:26,726 --> 00:36:28,978
-I'm back.
-Goodness!

733
00:36:29,062 --> 00:36:30,605
Oh my, you're here again.

734
00:36:31,272 --> 00:36:33,274
-[housekeeper 2] What's all this?
-[housekeeper 1] Why did you buy so much?

735
00:36:33,358 --> 00:36:35,652
I bought them in case you were hungry.

736
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:36,736
-One second.
-Goodness.

737
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:37,821
[housekeeper 3] What is all this?

738
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:40,824
Just leave it. We'll take care of this.

739
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:41,908
Hey, hey.

740
00:36:41,991 --> 00:36:45,078
Don't even lift a finger.
Please take a seat.

741
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:46,621
-[housekeeper 1] Oh my.
-Don't lift our fingers?

742
00:36:46,705 --> 00:36:47,872
[all chuckling]

743
00:36:47,956 --> 00:36:50,750
-Even my husband isn't this kind.
-What a treat.

744
00:36:50,834 --> 00:36:52,043
We're being spoiled.

745
00:36:52,627 --> 00:36:54,003
[housekeeper 3] Coffee, too?

746
00:36:54,087 --> 00:36:55,422
By the way, who is this?

747
00:36:56,005 --> 00:36:58,091
Ah. She's my team leader.

748
00:36:58,174 --> 00:36:59,426
Hello.

749
00:36:59,509 --> 00:37:01,344
-Hello.
-Hello.

750
00:37:01,428 --> 00:37:03,304
Here's your coffee.

751
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:04,806
-Take your coffee.
-Thank you.

752
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:06,641
[Isoo] All right, please enjoy.

753
00:37:07,142 --> 00:37:09,811
-[housekeeper 4] Thank you.
-This is my first time trying this.

754
00:37:10,562 --> 00:37:11,938
But it's from the bakery here.

755
00:37:12,021 --> 00:37:13,940
It's super expensive.

756
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:18,486
Hmm?

757
00:37:19,404 --> 00:37:20,405
This is insane.

758
00:37:21,448 --> 00:37:22,657
It's so good.

759
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:23,992
[all chuckle]

760
00:37:24,743 --> 00:37:26,119
It's really delicious.

761
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:28,246
Now I see why it's 100,000 won.

762
00:37:28,329 --> 00:37:29,664
You should have some, too.

763
00:37:29,748 --> 00:37:31,708
-Yes, have some.
-[Hyera chuckles]

764
00:37:32,125 --> 00:37:34,669
All right. If you insist, I won't say no.

765
00:37:34,753 --> 00:37:36,588
-[housekeeper 1] Go on, eat up.
-[women chuckle]

766
00:37:38,423 --> 00:37:39,591
Mmm. Mmm.

767
00:37:40,467 --> 00:37:42,135
-It's delicious.
-It is, isn't it?

768
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:43,803
[women chuckling]

769
00:37:45,013 --> 00:37:47,182
Uh, so, did you look into it?

770
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:49,976
We gathered all the information,

771
00:37:50,059 --> 00:37:51,060
just like you said.

772
00:37:51,144 --> 00:37:52,353
Go on, tell him.

773
00:37:53,855 --> 00:37:55,356
I heard this from security.

774
00:37:56,816 --> 00:37:58,610
He was on his way to work on Wednesday.

775
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:02,197
-[distant scuffle]
-[woman] I saw everything, you bitch!

776
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:04,491
You've got it all wrong. It's not me!

777
00:38:04,574 --> 00:38:06,534
You psycho bitch!

778
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:07,619
[♪ tense music playing]

779
00:38:07,702 --> 00:38:09,662
Hey, are you saying

780
00:38:09,746 --> 00:38:11,623
I'm delusional?

781
00:38:11,706 --> 00:38:12,957
You crazy...

782
00:38:13,041 --> 00:38:14,584
-Please calm down, ma'am.
-What?

783
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:16,127
Let go!

784
00:38:16,211 --> 00:38:17,837
Are you out of your damn minds?

785
00:38:17,921 --> 00:38:19,506
Hey, do your job properly!

786
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,591
Who do you think you are?

787
00:38:21,674 --> 00:38:23,885
Do you have any idea
who you're dealing with?

788
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:26,012
Wake the hell up! Hey, get on your knees.

789
00:38:26,095 --> 00:38:27,555
I said, kneel down.

790
00:38:27,639 --> 00:38:29,808
You crazy bitch! Kneel!

791
00:38:29,891 --> 00:38:31,434
Who was she?

792
00:38:31,518 --> 00:38:32,519
It was...

793
00:38:34,562 --> 00:38:35,688
the hotel owner's wife.

794
00:38:35,772 --> 00:38:36,773
Wait,

795
00:38:37,774 --> 00:38:41,361
the owner was dating Ms. Oh Minyeong?

796
00:38:41,444 --> 00:38:42,946
No, it's not that.

797
00:38:43,029 --> 00:38:46,032
There were rumors
that he was in love with her.

798
00:38:46,115 --> 00:38:49,077
I saw him following her around as well.

799
00:38:50,620 --> 00:38:52,705
[hotel owner] Wait,
we're not done talking.

800
00:38:54,457 --> 00:38:55,708
I have nothing else to say.

801
00:38:55,792 --> 00:38:57,669
I said we're not done.

802
00:38:57,752 --> 00:38:58,753
Let go.

803
00:38:59,295 --> 00:39:00,338
[soft thud]

804
00:39:07,470 --> 00:39:08,763
We'll talk later.

805
00:39:09,764 --> 00:39:11,015
[♪ music swells, fades]

806
00:39:15,353 --> 00:39:17,230
He tried to drag her into Room 709?

807
00:39:18,064 --> 00:39:20,233
Yes, it was really scary.

808
00:39:20,942 --> 00:39:23,570
I've never seen the boss like that before.

809
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:25,154
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

810
00:39:25,238 --> 00:39:28,700
Come to think of it,
there's something strange about Room 709.

811
00:39:28,783 --> 00:39:29,784
What do you mean?

812
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:31,953
Uh, about once a week,

813
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:34,497
we're asked to clean that room at dawn.

814
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,797
But when I looked into it,

815
00:39:44,007 --> 00:39:46,175
that room has been vacant for two months.

816
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:48,052
-[gasps]
-What on earth?

817
00:39:48,136 --> 00:39:49,596
[housekeeper 3] That's scary.

818
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,098
[Hyera sighs softly]

819
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:54,183
[no audio on footage]

820
00:39:58,771 --> 00:40:01,149
[door opens, closes]

821
00:40:02,609 --> 00:40:04,027
What's going on?

822
00:40:06,112 --> 00:40:08,740
There was an assault here last Wednesday.

823
00:40:08,823 --> 00:40:11,534
Shouldn't you have told us
something like this had happened?

824
00:40:12,493 --> 00:40:13,995
I didn't think it was relevant.

825
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:15,914
Not relevant?

826
00:40:15,997 --> 00:40:18,082
It looks like she wants to kill Ms. Oh.

827
00:40:18,666 --> 00:40:21,294
She looks pretty strong, too.
She's our first suspect.

828
00:40:21,377 --> 00:40:22,378
I doubt it.

829
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:24,797
She won't have killed her.

830
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:27,091
Why don't we check?

831
00:40:28,051 --> 00:40:29,844
What's her license plate number?

832
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:31,971
[surveillance operator] It's 0948.

833
00:40:32,055 --> 00:40:35,308
Can I see the parking garage entry log
from the day of the murder?

834
00:40:37,769 --> 00:40:38,937
Here you go.

835
00:40:45,944 --> 00:40:48,154
She came in at 7:42 p.m.

836
00:40:48,738 --> 00:40:51,783
Please show me
where she went after 7:42 p.m.

837
00:40:51,866 --> 00:40:53,868
[♪ gripping suspenseful music continues]

838
00:41:03,044 --> 00:41:04,170
[scoffs]

839
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:07,382
She even disguised herself.

840
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:10,635
I heard the hotel owner
was chasing after Ms. Oh.

841
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:12,929
There were rumors about that,

842
00:41:13,596 --> 00:41:14,806
but I don't know anything.

843
00:41:15,932 --> 00:41:17,976
Why was Room 709 left vacant?

844
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:20,853
I heard it was left
unoccupied for two months.

845
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:28,444
Oddly enough, it coincides with the time
the seventh-floor camera was broken.

846
00:41:28,528 --> 00:41:29,529
Two months.

847
00:41:30,238 --> 00:41:32,490
No, the camera wasn't broken.

848
00:41:36,536 --> 00:41:39,539
The central server stopped recording.

849
00:41:43,042 --> 00:41:44,627
Are you going to keep interfering?

850
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:48,047
Explain what happened.

851
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:50,008
[♪ music swells, fades]

852
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:58,057
I was following the CEO's orders.

853
00:41:58,141 --> 00:41:59,934
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

854
00:42:00,018 --> 00:42:01,519
The CEO's orders?

855
00:42:01,602 --> 00:42:02,603
Yes.

856
00:42:03,896 --> 00:42:07,734
He told me to turn off the security camera
and leave Room 709 unoccupied.

857
00:42:07,817 --> 00:42:08,818
For what reason?

858
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:11,404
I really don't know.

859
00:42:12,488 --> 00:42:13,573
Where is he right now?

860
00:42:15,450 --> 00:42:16,701
He has a prior commitment,

861
00:42:17,994 --> 00:42:19,412
so he'll be in this afternoon.

862
00:42:19,495 --> 00:42:20,705
[♪ music swells]

863
00:42:23,583 --> 00:42:24,667
[♪ music fades]

864
00:42:24,751 --> 00:42:27,378
The hotel owner also stalked
Ms. Oh Minyeong?

865
00:42:28,838 --> 00:42:31,215
His wife suspected
they were having an affair

866
00:42:31,299 --> 00:42:32,800
and assaulted Ms. Oh Minyeong.

867
00:42:32,884 --> 00:42:36,220
On the day of the murder, his wife
and daughter came here in disguise.

868
00:42:36,304 --> 00:42:37,346
[scoffs]

869
00:42:37,430 --> 00:42:39,682
What on earth is going on?

870
00:42:40,683 --> 00:42:43,227
Room 709 was left vacant for two months.

871
00:42:43,311 --> 00:42:44,979
On the owner's orders.

872
00:42:45,063 --> 00:42:48,775
The owner, Yeom Jaeseop, left more
prints at the scene than anyone else.

873
00:42:48,858 --> 00:42:50,610
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

874
00:42:50,693 --> 00:42:53,112
YEOM JAESEOP'S FINGERPRINTS
DETECTED MOST FREQUENTLY

875
00:42:53,196 --> 00:42:57,408
What was he doing with the security camera
off and that room left vacant?

876
00:42:57,492 --> 00:42:59,035
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

877
00:42:59,118 --> 00:43:01,412
He's coming in the afternoon,
so you two find out.

878
00:43:01,496 --> 00:43:03,664
-We'll go meet his wife.
-Got it.

879
00:43:03,748 --> 00:43:06,459
Don't push him too hard.
Just see what he says.

880
00:43:06,542 --> 00:43:07,835
Understood.

881
00:43:07,919 --> 00:43:09,378
[engine roaring]

882
00:43:10,630 --> 00:43:12,090
[engine downshifts, brakes squeal]

883
00:43:12,965 --> 00:43:14,008
[ignition clicks off]

884
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,519
[gate bell chimes]

885
00:43:28,648 --> 00:43:30,691
I'm Joo Hyera, with Gangha Police.

886
00:43:33,069 --> 00:43:35,238
You must've seen
the dermatologist this morning.

887
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:36,322
[sighs]

888
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:37,406
WIFE OF YEOM JAESEOP
CHA SERAN

889
00:43:37,490 --> 00:43:39,075
I can't take these off yet.

890
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:42,245
What's this about?

891
00:43:42,328 --> 00:43:44,872
What else could it be?
That bitch must've reported us.

892
00:43:44,956 --> 00:43:46,791
Are you talking about Ms. Oh Minyeong?

893
00:43:46,874 --> 00:43:49,127
She can sue me if she wants.
I'll do the same.

894
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:51,295
That shameless bitch.

895
00:43:51,379 --> 00:43:53,089
[sighs] What's got you so upset?

896
00:43:53,172 --> 00:43:54,966
[sighs] Don't even get me started.

897
00:43:55,550 --> 00:43:57,802
Just thinking about it
makes my blood boil.

898
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:01,514
I should've just killed her back then.

899
00:44:01,597 --> 00:44:03,057
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

900
00:44:10,857 --> 00:44:12,275
We're with Gangha Police.

901
00:44:12,900 --> 00:44:14,443
Is the CEO inside?

902
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:21,450
OWNER OF ROSEBUD HOTEL
YEOM JAESEOP

903
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:25,413
Are you aware that Ms. Oh Minyeong died?

904
00:44:27,081 --> 00:44:28,249
Yes, I heard.

905
00:44:28,332 --> 00:44:30,751
She was murdered in Room 709.

906
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:34,422
[Seran] I have this friend.

907
00:44:34,505 --> 00:44:36,465
She runs a luxury boutique.

908
00:44:37,383 --> 00:44:40,970
She said my husband asked her
to find him a limited-edition handbag.

909
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:44,056
I assumed it was a gift for me and waited.

910
00:44:46,893 --> 00:44:47,894
Look at this.

911
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:53,316
[scoffs] He gave it to that bitch.

912
00:44:53,399 --> 00:44:55,651
How could I not lose it after seeing that?

913
00:44:56,694 --> 00:44:57,862
How did you take these?

914
00:44:57,945 --> 00:45:00,031
He's been acting strange
for a few months now.

915
00:45:00,740 --> 00:45:03,618
He couldn't stop smiling
and had his head in the clouds.

916
00:45:04,785 --> 00:45:07,705
I figured he was seeing another woman
and had him followed.

917
00:45:08,789 --> 00:45:12,168
His office is visible
from the building next to the hotel.

918
00:45:12,960 --> 00:45:14,712
Is she going to sue me?

919
00:45:14,795 --> 00:45:16,297
After doing this behind my back?

920
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:18,633
That evil bitch.

921
00:45:21,636 --> 00:45:22,762
Ms. Oh Minyeong

922
00:45:23,721 --> 00:45:24,847
is deceased.

923
00:45:24,931 --> 00:45:26,265
What?

924
00:45:29,477 --> 00:45:31,520
She was murdered
at the hotel two nights ago.

925
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:36,484
In Room 709?

926
00:45:37,360 --> 00:45:38,361
Yes.

927
00:45:38,444 --> 00:45:41,697
We heard you instructed the staff
to keep that room vacant.

928
00:45:41,781 --> 00:45:42,823
Yes.

929
00:45:45,284 --> 00:45:48,204
I kept that room for my own personal use.

930
00:45:48,287 --> 00:45:50,289
Your personal use?

931
00:45:50,373 --> 00:45:53,334
We're getting ready to open
a new hotel in Gangbuk.

932
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:55,836
I had a lot of work,
so I often stayed the night here.

933
00:45:55,920 --> 00:45:58,506
So I kept a room aside for my own use.

934
00:45:59,340 --> 00:46:02,385
But it's peak season soon,
so I told them to reopen it on the 14th.

935
00:46:03,010 --> 00:46:06,097
Why would Ms. Oh Minyeong
have died in that room?

936
00:46:08,516 --> 00:46:09,767
I wouldn't know.

937
00:46:11,394 --> 00:46:15,773
There are rumors
that you had feelings for her.

938
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:19,777
You even bought her a designer handbag.

939
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:20,987
[sighs defeatedly]

940
00:46:23,698 --> 00:46:26,075
Yes, well, I suppose I did.

941
00:46:27,785 --> 00:46:29,578
But I didn't do anything to her.

942
00:46:30,371 --> 00:46:31,789
I swear.

943
00:46:33,666 --> 00:46:36,168
At 7:42 p.m. that day,

944
00:46:36,252 --> 00:46:37,712
you two came to the hotel.

945
00:46:39,755 --> 00:46:42,341
Here, look. With your faces covered,
acting suspiciously.

946
00:46:42,425 --> 00:46:43,759
It's all on camera.

947
00:46:45,386 --> 00:46:48,306
Wait, are you saying

948
00:46:49,140 --> 00:46:50,766
that we killed that bitch?

949
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:53,602
-It wasn't us.
-Why did you go to the hotel?

950
00:46:56,689 --> 00:46:58,941
Are you aware
that your wife assaulted Ms. Oh?

951
00:47:00,192 --> 00:47:02,820
My wife misunderstood.
She's pathologically jealous.

952
00:47:03,446 --> 00:47:05,364
Ms. Oh must've been really angry.

953
00:47:06,532 --> 00:47:09,702
Yes, so I agreed to transfer her
to the new hotel as a manager.

954
00:47:09,785 --> 00:47:11,871
[scoffs, inhales deeply]

955
00:47:11,954 --> 00:47:13,122
Of all places,

956
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:16,459
a murder happened in Room 709,
the one you used personally,

957
00:47:16,542 --> 00:47:17,877
and of all times,

958
00:47:17,960 --> 00:47:20,046
the camera on the seventh floor is down,

959
00:47:20,129 --> 00:47:21,922
so we can't seem to identify a suspect.

960
00:47:24,675 --> 00:47:26,344
The security camera is down?

961
00:47:29,305 --> 00:47:30,723
I didn't know that.

962
00:47:38,397 --> 00:47:41,609
"I'll kill Oh Minyeong and go to hell."

963
00:47:42,318 --> 00:47:44,195
-That's what you thought, no?
-No.

964
00:47:44,278 --> 00:47:47,198
We were only
trying to catch them in the act.

965
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:48,616
Kill her?

966
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:51,577
-What a horrible thing to say.
-[phone clatters on table]

967
00:47:52,411 --> 00:47:54,663
-Then why did you go there?
-Well,

968
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:56,540
my husband

969
00:47:57,124 --> 00:48:00,836
swore up and down that it wasn't true
and promised he'd start coming home early.

970
00:48:02,338 --> 00:48:06,008
But that afternoon, he didn't answer
his phone or come home.

971
00:48:06,759 --> 00:48:10,012
They were together again
because it was White Day.

972
00:48:10,846 --> 00:48:12,765
[exhales deeply] White Day, again.

973
00:48:12,848 --> 00:48:14,850
I'm starting to hate White Day.

974
00:48:15,476 --> 00:48:16,560
So?

975
00:48:17,228 --> 00:48:18,479
[♪ foreboding music playing]

976
00:48:18,562 --> 00:48:19,855
[Seran] I went to his office,

977
00:48:21,774 --> 00:48:22,775
but he wasn't there.

978
00:48:22,858 --> 00:48:25,027
-Where did he go?
-Let's go, Mom.

979
00:48:25,694 --> 00:48:27,154
That man, I swear.

980
00:48:28,114 --> 00:48:31,200
So I went to the security office
and searched through the footage.

981
00:48:40,668 --> 00:48:42,086
Where is he going?

982
00:48:42,169 --> 00:48:43,462
And I saw him

983
00:48:43,546 --> 00:48:45,256
go down to the seventh floor.

984
00:48:46,841 --> 00:48:48,050
At what time?

985
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:52,513
[scoffs] Are you kidding me?

986
00:48:52,596 --> 00:48:55,808
Around 7:50 p.m.?

987
00:48:55,891 --> 00:48:57,518
Yeah, it was 7:50 p.m.

988
00:48:57,601 --> 00:49:00,354
[Seran] Right. We missed him by a hair.

989
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:04,817
So I rang every doorbell.

990
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:06,444
[doorbells ringing]

991
00:49:07,528 --> 00:49:09,321
-Where is he hiding?
-Where are they?

992
00:49:11,282 --> 00:49:12,366
Come out here!

993
00:49:14,160 --> 00:49:15,786
Where are you? [exclaims]

994
00:49:15,870 --> 00:49:18,164
-Dad!
-Come out.

995
00:49:18,247 --> 00:49:19,248
Right now!

996
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:21,876
I went back to the security office,

997
00:49:21,959 --> 00:49:23,502
and he was on the 10th floor.

998
00:49:24,211 --> 00:49:25,546
So I went there...

999
00:49:26,505 --> 00:49:28,090
[sighs] ...and he was there.

1000
00:49:28,174 --> 00:49:29,508
What time was that?

1001
00:49:29,592 --> 00:49:31,260
It was 8...

1002
00:49:31,343 --> 00:49:33,554
Around 8:20 p.m.

1003
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:36,640
[sharp inhale]
You'll get into trouble if you lie to us.

1004
00:49:36,724 --> 00:49:39,059
I'm not lying.
The front desk clerk was there, too.

1005
00:49:39,143 --> 00:49:40,269
Yes, you're right.

1006
00:49:40,352 --> 00:49:41,562
That good-looking kid.

1007
00:49:41,645 --> 00:49:43,272
[Jaeseop] Then you leave!

1008
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:45,316
Jaeseop.

1009
00:49:54,575 --> 00:49:57,203
[angrily] Where were you? [exclaims]

1010
00:49:57,870 --> 00:49:59,121
He was being scolded.

1011
00:50:02,708 --> 00:50:04,251
I'm telling the truth!

1012
00:50:05,127 --> 00:50:07,963
[scoffs incredulously]
How could I possibly kill someone?

1013
00:50:08,047 --> 00:50:09,173
God, seriously...

1014
00:50:09,882 --> 00:50:11,884
It wasn't me. I didn't kill her.

1015
00:50:12,468 --> 00:50:13,636
I didn't!

1016
00:50:13,719 --> 00:50:15,679
Then why did you disguise yourself?

1017
00:50:15,763 --> 00:50:16,889
Uh...

1018
00:50:16,972 --> 00:50:20,392
How could I show up there
after the scene I made last week?

1019
00:50:20,476 --> 00:50:21,560
I have to save face.

1020
00:50:22,144 --> 00:50:23,437
[Isoo scoffs]

1021
00:50:23,521 --> 00:50:26,065
You grabbed her by the hair,
but you want to save face?

1022
00:50:26,148 --> 00:50:27,566
You'll see when you're married.

1023
00:50:27,650 --> 00:50:30,486
It's not easy keeping an eye on
such a successful husband. [sighs]

1024
00:50:30,569 --> 00:50:33,656
CEO MINDSET
DESIGNING THE VALUE OF STAYS

1025
00:50:35,366 --> 00:50:37,201
Detective Park? Still at the hotel?

1026
00:50:37,284 --> 00:50:38,744
[Junyoung] Yes.

1027
00:50:38,827 --> 00:50:42,665
At 8:20 p.m., Mr. Yeom was supposedly
with the front desk clerk in his office.

1028
00:50:43,332 --> 00:50:45,334
-Verify that for me.
-Okay, got it.

1029
00:50:46,168 --> 00:50:50,214
At around 8:20 p.m. on the 13th,
did you go to the CEO's office?

1030
00:50:51,340 --> 00:50:53,634
Yes. He wanted to see me.

1031
00:50:54,593 --> 00:50:55,886
Why do you ask?

1032
00:50:55,970 --> 00:50:58,013
[chuckles]
We're just verifying statements.

1033
00:50:58,597 --> 00:51:01,308
Did you see the CEO's wife
and his daughter there?

1034
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:03,894
Yes. They came in together.

1035
00:51:07,147 --> 00:51:09,692
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

1036
00:51:09,775 --> 00:51:11,318
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

1037
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:13,529
MARRIED
SUSPECTS AFFAIR

1038
00:51:15,322 --> 00:51:17,700
8:00 P.M.,
ESTIMATED TIME OF DEATH, 9:00 P.M.

1039
00:51:24,498 --> 00:51:27,376
[sharp inhale] I've got this feeling
Yeom Jaeseop is our guy.

1040
00:51:28,168 --> 00:51:29,712
He does seem suspicious.

1041
00:51:29,795 --> 00:51:31,297
And his statement doesn't add up.

1042
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:34,800
He killed an employee he stalked
inside his own hotel?

1043
00:51:34,883 --> 00:51:36,844
In the room he used, no less?

1044
00:51:36,927 --> 00:51:38,220
Maybe it doesn't make sense.

1045
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:41,056
What about his wife?

1046
00:51:42,099 --> 00:51:43,142
She was paranoid.

1047
00:51:43,225 --> 00:51:46,228
She would've heard about
the broken camera at the security office.

1048
00:51:46,812 --> 00:51:49,023
Who would kill someone
they assaulted a week ago?

1049
00:51:49,106 --> 00:51:50,232
Unless they're an idiot.

1050
00:51:50,983 --> 00:51:53,277
Nothing seems to add up, huh?

1051
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:56,280
[sharp inhale] There's no motive,

1052
00:51:56,363 --> 00:51:57,698
and no murder weapon.

1053
00:51:57,781 --> 00:51:58,949
Detective Joo.

1054
00:52:01,243 --> 00:52:03,162
-You said the bloodstains were small.
-[Hyera] Yes.

1055
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:05,539
[forensics officer] We took the carpet in
for testing,

1056
00:52:05,623 --> 00:52:07,082
and there wasn't enough blood.

1057
00:52:07,916 --> 00:52:10,169
We checked thoroughly,
but found no blood spatter.

1058
00:52:10,878 --> 00:52:13,047
I don't think she was murdered here.

1059
00:52:13,130 --> 00:52:14,965
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

1060
00:52:18,636 --> 00:52:19,928
She died somewhere else?

1061
00:52:20,012 --> 00:52:21,972
Did the culprit move the body?

1062
00:52:22,056 --> 00:52:24,099
Huh? That's so creepy.

1063
00:52:24,183 --> 00:52:27,436
Then they wiped the blood
with hydrogen peroxide.

1064
00:52:27,519 --> 00:52:28,562
HYDROGEN PEROXIDE DETECTED

1065
00:52:30,064 --> 00:52:31,357
[sighs deeply]

1066
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:33,359
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1067
00:52:35,486 --> 00:52:36,945
[line ringing over car audio]

1068
00:52:38,280 --> 00:52:40,407
-Ma'am, I have a favor to ask.
-[housekeeper] Okay.

1069
00:52:40,491 --> 00:52:42,951
Ms. Oh was murdered somewhere else.

1070
00:52:43,035 --> 00:52:46,038
Please find out if anyone saw
anything unusual while cleaning.

1071
00:52:46,121 --> 00:52:47,373
Okay, got it.

1072
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:49,708
[line disconnects]

1073
00:52:51,669 --> 00:52:53,087
[engine roaring]

1074
00:52:55,297 --> 00:52:57,007
Oh my goodness. [breathing heavily]

1075
00:53:00,135 --> 00:53:02,137
-[radio beeps]
-This is your manager.

1076
00:53:02,221 --> 00:53:05,599
We have an urgent request
from Detective Jin Isoo.

1077
00:53:05,683 --> 00:53:07,518
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

1078
00:53:09,436 --> 00:53:11,438
-[remote beeps]
-[motorized curtains whirring]

1079
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:40,759
Are you checking out?

1080
00:53:42,594 --> 00:53:43,929
[keyboard clacking]

1081
00:53:46,640 --> 00:53:47,933
[sighs softly]

1082
00:53:49,685 --> 00:53:50,686
[remote beeps]

1083
00:54:08,412 --> 00:54:09,913
What's this?

1084
00:54:11,081 --> 00:54:12,082
[sniffs]

1085
00:54:15,961 --> 00:54:17,629
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1086
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:30,601
[clerk] Your payment's all set.

1087
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:34,521
Your car is waiting outside.

1088
00:54:48,160 --> 00:54:49,745
[♪ music swells]

1089
00:54:52,498 --> 00:54:53,499
[♪ music fades]

1090
00:54:58,795 --> 00:54:59,796
SECRET AGENT DELTA

1091
00:55:01,673 --> 00:55:04,259
-[digital beep]
-Yes, Ms. Delta.

1092
00:55:05,344 --> 00:55:07,137
[♪ ominous music playing]

1093
00:55:07,221 --> 00:55:09,598
Detective Jin, it's Room 701.

1094
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:10,766
Room 701?

1095
00:55:11,683 --> 00:55:12,976
What about Room 701?

1096
00:55:13,060 --> 00:55:14,269
[Ms. Delta] I came in to clean,

1097
00:55:15,562 --> 00:55:17,523
and I found something
that looks like blood.

1098
00:55:17,606 --> 00:55:18,857
What?

1099
00:55:18,941 --> 00:55:20,901
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

1100
00:55:23,570 --> 00:55:25,405
[flesh squelching]

1101
00:55:28,450 --> 00:55:29,660
[blood splatters]

1102
00:55:35,415 --> 00:55:36,667
Kang Chunsik.

1103
00:55:39,211 --> 00:55:40,879
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1104
00:55:42,506 --> 00:55:43,674
[swears softly]

1105
00:55:44,383 --> 00:55:45,842
[engine roaring, tires screech]

1106
00:55:57,771 --> 00:55:59,022
[Hyera] Watch out!

1107
00:55:59,106 --> 00:56:01,650
Don't worry. My car's more expensive.

1108
00:56:02,901 --> 00:56:05,571
[scoffs] How dare he try to take me on?

1109
00:56:06,822 --> 00:56:07,864
[grunts softly]

1110
00:56:08,615 --> 00:56:09,866
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

1111
00:56:09,950 --> 00:56:11,368
-[siren blaring]
-[Isoo exclaims smugly]

1112
00:56:19,126 --> 00:56:20,168
[tires screech]

1113
00:56:22,087 --> 00:56:23,255
[engine roaring]

1114
00:56:33,974 --> 00:56:34,975
Hey, hey.

1115
00:56:35,058 --> 00:56:36,893
Vehicle ahead, stop the car.

1116
00:56:37,686 --> 00:56:40,188
The trust-fund kid in car 6383!

1117
00:56:40,272 --> 00:56:41,815
Stop the car!

1118
00:56:43,900 --> 00:56:45,527
Stop the car!

1119
00:56:47,404 --> 00:56:48,572
[tires screech]

1120
00:56:54,786 --> 00:56:55,954
My good citizens!

1121
00:56:56,038 --> 00:56:58,040
Chunsik Food's sole heir is on the run!

1122
00:56:58,749 --> 00:57:01,168
We are police.

1123
00:57:01,251 --> 00:57:03,879
Kang Chunsik is on the run!

1124
00:57:04,546 --> 00:57:06,465
Kang Chunsik, stop the damn car!

1125
00:57:06,548 --> 00:57:07,674
[sighs defeatedly]

1126
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:09,968
[tires screeching]

1127
00:57:10,052 --> 00:57:11,261
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

1128
00:57:11,345 --> 00:57:13,889
That brat just won't listen.

1129
00:57:15,182 --> 00:57:16,266
Here we go.

1130
00:57:16,350 --> 00:57:18,018
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

1131
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:19,770
[siren continues blaring]

1132
00:57:19,853 --> 00:57:20,854
[tires screech]

1133
00:57:34,868 --> 00:57:36,578
[tires screeching]

1134
00:57:50,967 --> 00:57:52,386
[engine revving]

1135
00:57:54,638 --> 00:57:55,681
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 5

1136
00:57:55,764 --> 00:57:57,474
DO THE BLOODSTAINS POINT
TO KANG CHUNSIK?

1137
00:57:57,557 --> 00:57:59,559
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1138
00:58:22,082 --> 00:58:25,502
Special Cast.
Special Cast. Choi Dukmoon, Lee Suk

1139
00:58:25,585 --> 00:58:29,005
Special Cast.
Ko Gunhan, Seo Hyewon

1140
00:58:32,592 --> 00:58:33,593
Look who's busted.

1141
00:58:33,677 --> 00:58:35,887
-Minyeong died in my hotel room?
-[thud]

1142
00:58:35,971 --> 00:58:37,889
[sobbing] Do you have any idea
how much I loved her?

1143
00:58:38,348 --> 00:58:39,808
If that was an act, she deserves an Oscar.

1144
00:58:39,891 --> 00:58:41,059
Are you going to keep lying?

1145
00:58:41,143 --> 00:58:43,019
There's only an eight-minute gap.

1146
00:58:43,103 --> 00:58:45,397
-That's impossible, isn't it?
-It's impossible without an accomplice.

1147
00:58:45,480 --> 00:58:47,566
-[Kyungjin] Yeom Jaeseop left the country!
-You have a private jet.

1148
00:58:47,649 --> 00:58:49,735
Captain! We're off to Hanoi!

1149
00:58:49,818 --> 00:58:51,570
Jin Isoo is here!

1150
00:58:51,653 --> 00:58:52,988
Did you kill her? [exclaims]

1151
00:58:53,071 --> 00:58:54,197
[Isoo] Come on, seriously?

1152
00:58:54,281 --> 00:58:55,991
We met secretly in Room 709.

1153
00:58:56,450 --> 00:58:58,201
-Let's end this.
-Stop what?

1154
00:58:58,285 --> 00:58:59,786
She was definitely alive
when I left the room.

1155
00:58:59,870 --> 00:59:01,955
Someone was trying to frame me.

1156
00:59:07,878 --> 00:59:09,629
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1157
00:59:19,097 --> 00:59:20,807
-Mr. Hwang.
-[both chuckling]

1158
00:59:20,891 --> 00:59:22,642
Young master. You're here.

1159
00:59:22,726 --> 00:59:24,686
You've gotten old.

1160
00:59:25,187 --> 00:59:27,147
-Did you clean the place?
-Yes, of course.

1161
00:59:28,857 --> 00:59:30,317
Go on inside.

1162
00:59:40,660 --> 00:59:42,454
[♪ ominous music playing]

1163
01:00:09,981 --> 01:00:11,316
[exhales softly]

1164
01:00:13,443 --> 01:00:15,862
[♪ melancholy piano music playing
over record player]

1165
01:00:43,557 --> 01:00:45,559
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
